{"ts":"2026-10-10T12:02:00.063Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01KkwKz5kkbVuKpPniJUfWgV","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\activeContext.md","result":" 1 | # Active context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Current state (after T4, trimmed)\n 4 | T4 is done (items 1–4; polish = loading state on `/` only). 264 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean.\n 5 | - **Admin passcode:** optional `ADMIN_PASSCODE` in `.env.local`. When set, `/api/admin/*` needs the header `x-admin-passcode` (`src/server/adminAuth.ts`, 401 otherwise) and `/admin` shows a passcode box (kept in sessionStorage). When not set, `/admin` shows an amber \"Demo mode: unprotected\" banner.\n 6 | - **Guardrails audit:** `src/guardrails.test.ts` (renders ReportStep/CoverSheet/CheckItem to static HTML + scans the source). One fix: the printed cover sheet now prints \"Source · verified on · Provisional rule\" per listed check. The checklist is in `tasks/LOG.md`.\n 7 | - **Rejection decoder** `/decode`: textarea → `POST /api/decode` → `ai.ts classifyRejection()` (zod `RawClassification`: one `RejectionCode` + confidence) → pure `decodeResult()` in `src/core/decode.ts`. ≥ 0.7 and not UNKNOWN → matched, with the fixed steps from `rejectionCodes.ts`; otherwise needs verification + `ASK_AT_OFFICE`. Digits are redacted before the model sees them. Linked from home (\"Got a rejection? Decode it\"). Works without AI (needs verification).\n 8 | - **`npm run demo:reset`:** `scripts/demo-reset.mjs` → `RuleStore.resetAll()` (one transaction). A running server drops the reset versions on its next request (`syncRegistry` → `resetRegistry`). The real `data/kaagaz.db` was reset in this run (it had 2 old proposals).\n 9 | - **`AgeRange.max` is optional** (no upper limit, \"60 or older\").\n10 | \n11 | ## Decisions made in T4\n12 | - The passcode protects the API (the real boundary); the page itself is just a shell. Constant-time compare on SHA-256 digests; the passcode is never logged or echoed.\n13 | - The decoder's model only classifies; the status, steps and questions are code. A low-confidence guess is shown only as \"It might be: … please confirm at the office\".\n14 | - `demo-reset.mjs` imports `src/server/store.ts` directly (Node 24 type stripping, `--disable-warning=MODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON`) so `store.ts` stays the only DB writer.\n15 | - The new Assamese strings (`decode.*`, `ASK_AT_OFFICE`, \"বা তাতকৈ বেছি\") are drafts.\n16 | \n17 | ## Next step\n18 | T-last: freeze, README (a `docs/README-draft.md` exists, not by Cline), demo path check incl. 360px + phone click-through of `/`, `/admin`, `/decode`; native-speaker review of the Assamese.\n19 | \n20 | ## Previous state (after T3)\n21 | T3 is done: the **Rule Maintenance Agent** works end to end against the live Cline API. On `/admin` a maintainer pastes a notice or loads a demo notice. A `@cline/sdk` Agent works only through 5 tools (`getRuleSchema`, `getCurrentRule`, `proposeRule`, `runTests`, `saveProposal`), and the page shows a live tool-call log, a readable before/after diff, test results (new + regression), Publish / Reject, and version history per scheme. Published versions are live at once in `/` and `/api/check`, and the old versions are kept.\n22 | Live run (smoke, 2026-10-10): the IGNOAPS notice gave new scheme `nsap-old-age` 1.0.0 (5/5 new tests); the Orunodoi notice gave `orunodoi-3` 2.0.0 → 2.1.0 with an Oct 1–31 2026 override (4 new + 4 regression tests pass). After publishing, `/api/check` returns 1500 on 2026-10-15 and 1250 on 2026-11-15, and the home page lists the Old Age Pension.\n23 | 225 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean.\n24 | \n25 | ## Decisions made in T3\n26 | - \"Type it in\": a document counts only once its main field has a value (`MAIN_FIELD` in `docFields.ts`, `isDocAdded` / `countedDocs` in `flow.ts`). Death certificate and BPL proof (nothing is read from them) count as soon as they are added. Only counted docs go to `/api/check` and onto the cover sheet; a started-but-empty slot shows \"Type the name on the next screen to add it\".\n27 | - Code decides everything about a proposal (`rulePolicy.ts`): the version must go up; ≥ 3 new tests with unique ids; a provenance may be `verified` only if it is carried over unchanged or its `sourceUrl` appears in the notice. Otherwise it must be `provisional`, so the engine says needs_verification. `saveProposal` is refused unless every new and regression test passes. `publish` re-runs all checks (a stale proposal cannot go live).\n28 | - Regression tests = built-in suites (`schemes/regression.ts`, the \"version 1\" tests) + the tests of every published version of that scheme.\n29 | - The agent edits existing schemes with a JSON merge patch (`mergePatch.ts`, RFC 7386) instead of re-sending the whole rule (fewer tokens, faster demo).\n30 | - `ai.ts` also hosts `runToolAgent` (the agent path), so there is still one model module: it logs model / promptVersion / inputHash / toolCalls, retries once only if no tool ran yet, falls back to `{ error }`, and never throws.\n31 | - Store = `node:sqlite` file (`KAAGAZ_DB_PATH` or `data/kaagaz.db`). `rule_versions` has extra `notice` and `summary` columns (needed to re-check provenance at publish time and to show the reviewer a summary). A unique partial index allows one published row per scheme+version.\n32 | - `/` and `/admin` render per request (`connection()` inside `<Suspense>`); every request calls `syncRegistry()` (idempotent), so versions published by any process appear immediately.\n33 | - `/admin` is English-only (for maintainers, not citizens). There is no auth on `/admin`; see Requests for Claude in LOG.md.\n34 | \n35 | ## Previous state (after T2)\n36 | T2 (main flow) is done. One mobile flow on `/` (client component `src/app/_components/KaagazApp.tsx`): scheme cards (PM-KISAN first, \"flagship\") → documents (photo per slot via `/api/extract`, \"type it in\", or samples A/B/C with a purple \"Demo mode: fake sample documents\" label) → confirm fields (low confidence in amber) → big Yes/No questions → report from `/api/check`. The report shows the Eligibility banner, the Readiness banner (+ \"check at the bank\" list), Fix before you apply, Please verify, OK (collapsed), benefit (central / state top-up separately), supporting docs, a print-only cover sheet and the bilingual disclaimer. Assamese default, English toggle (`src/i18n.ts`).\n37 | 150 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean. The live Cline API reads a fake Aadhaar image correctly (image input works).\n38 | \n39 | ## Decisions made in T2\n40 | - `src/server/ai.ts` is the only model caller: `extractDocument(image, hint?, deps?)` → `{ doc, detectedDocType } | { error: ai_unavailable | ai_failed | invalid_image }`, one retry, logs only model/promptVersion/inputHash/outcome. The Cline API wraps responses as `{ data: { choices } }`; both shapes are handled.\n41 | - Raw model JSON → `ExtractedDoc` in pure `src/core/extraction.ts` (full Aadhaar → last 4; unscored AI fields → 0.5 confidence so they get confirmed; non-ISO DOB → low confidence).\n42 | - Route files do NOT export `runtime = \"nodejs\"`: Next 16.4 rejects it with `cacheComponents` (Node is the default anyway). Awaiting Claude's confirmation.\n43 | - Nothing is read from the death certificate or BPL proof (presence only); `husbandName` is not collected.\n44 | - The client never imports the engine: UI helpers live in `flow.ts`, `reportView.ts`, `catalog.ts`, `thresholds.ts`; the page (a server component) passes a plain `SchemeView[]` catalog.\n45 | - \"Type it in\" adds an empty document (counted as present by the engine); flagged for Claude.\n46 | \n47 | ## Decisions made in T1\n48 | - Brief v2: **Assamese default + English**; two verdicts (eligibility, readiness); provenance on every rule (verified vs provisional).\n49 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable, but a `verified` rule must have one (schema refine). Provisional overrides from the T3 agent can start with `sourceUrl: null`.\n50 | - `ExtractedDoc.fields` is strict and only holds `aadhaarLast4` (never a full Aadhaar number). A missing per-field confidence means \"entered/confirmed by the user\"; < 0.8 → needs_verification.\n51 | - The name reference document is Aadhaar for PM-KISAN and the widow pension, and the ration card for Orunodoi.\n52 | - A PM-KISAN land-owner mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (not ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes (farmer family = spouse/minor children).\n53 | - Orunodoi question ids: `nfsa_enrolled` (requirement); any-of `widow | person_with_disability | aay_card | income_below_2_lakh`; exclusions `elected_representative | professional | govt_staff_or_pensioner | contractor_or_trader | large_landholder | four_wheeler | similar_state_scheme`. All provisional.\n54 | - Widow pension: all mandatory docs (incl. `bpl_proof`) are provisional (\"commonly required; confirm locally\"); age and BPL are verified.\n55 | - The registry is in-memory: `registerScheme` validates, rejects a duplicate id+version and keeps old versions. T3 will persist versions in SQLite and register them at startup.\n56 | - Assamese strings in `labels.ts`, the scheme packs and `rejectionCodes.ts` are drafts awaiting native-speaker review (Das).\n57 | \n58 | ","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md","result":" 1 | # Progress\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Done\n 4 | - [x] T0: Memory Bank, Next.js 16 scaffold (TS strict, Tailwind v4, ESLint), Vitest + fast-check + zod, npm scripts, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, placeholder page, smoke test, first commit.\n 5 | - [x] T1: core rule engine v2. Step 0 (memory bank refreshed for brief v2; title \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", taglines EN/AS, `<html lang=\"as\">`); zod types; 3 rule packs with provenance + versioned registry; name matcher (Devanagari + Assamese/Bengali transliteration, Jaro-Winkler); `ageOn`; `maskAadhaar`; `benefitOn` with overrides; `evaluate` with two verdicts; rejection codes EN/AS; samples A/B/C. 93 tests.\n 6 | \n 7 | - [x] T2: main flow. `src/server/ai.ts` (Cline API vision, zod, one retry, `{ error }` fallback), `/api/extract` + `/api/check`, pure helpers (`extraction`, `flow`, `reportView`, `catalog`), `src/i18n.ts` (as/en), mobile UI (scheme → docs/samples → confirm → questions → two-verdict report → print cover sheet). 150 tests.\n 8 | \n 9 | - [x] T3: \"type it in\" fix (doc counts only once its main field is filled) + Rule Maintenance Agent: `@cline/sdk` Agent with 5 zod tools, `node:sqlite` store (`rule_versions`, WAL, transactions), pure rule tests / diff / policy / merge patch, admin API (NDJSON stream, list, publish, reject), `/admin` UI (demo notices, live log, diff, tests, Publish/Reject, history), `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs`. Both demo notices verified live. 225 tests.\n10 | \n11 | - [x] T4 (trimmed): optional admin passcode (`ADMIN_PASSCODE` → `x-admin-passcode` on `/api/admin/*`; passcode box / \"Demo mode: unprotected\" banner), guardrails audit (`src/guardrails.test.ts`; cover sheet now prints source + verified on), rejection decoder `/decode` (`classifyRejection` in ai.ts → pure `decodeResult`, ≥ 0.7 or needs verification + what to ask), `npm run demo:reset`, optional `AgeRange.max`. 264 tests.\n12 | \n13 | ## To do\n14 | - [ ] T-last: freeze, full README, demo path check (incl. 360px + phone click-through of `/`, `/admin`, `/decode`)\n15 | \n16 | ## Future scope\n17 | - Age-banded payments (e.g. IGNOAPS ₹200 for 60–79, ₹500 for 80+): the engine has one flat benefit per scheme; would need benefit bands keyed by age. Not now (Claude, T4).\n18 | - Decoder: photo of a rejection letter, and an AI-drafted correction/grievance letter (cut in T4).\n19 | - Assamese voice readout (only with a real as-IN voice).\n20 | \n21 | ## Known issues\n22 | - `npm install` warns that eslint@9 is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0). Harmless.\n23 | - Assamese strings (incl. all of `src/i18n.ts`) are drafts; they need native-speaker review before the demo.\n24 | - The T2 UI has not been clicked through on a real phone yet (only HTML + API smoke tests).\n25 | - Route files omit `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"` (incompatible with `cacheComponents` in Next 16.4); approved by Claude in T3.\n26 | - `/admin` is open unless `ADMIN_PASSCODE` is set in `.env.local` (then the API needs the passcode; the page shows a passcode box). Set it for any shared deployment.\n27 | - The engine has one flat benefit amount per scheme, so IGNOAPS's ₹500/month for ages 80+ can only be a note (see Future scope).\n28 | - The T3 agent prompt does not yet say that `ageRange.max` may be omitted (asked Claude).\n29 | - A live agent run takes about 20–60 s; the UI streams each tool call so the wait is visible.\n30 | - `npm install` warns that `protobufjs` (a dependency of `@cline/sdk`) has an unapproved postinstall script. Harmless; nothing is broken.\n31 | - The transliteration table is basic (good enough for possible_match on common names; cross-script is never `same`).","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\projectbrief.md","result":" 1 | # Project brief v2: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | **Pitch:** We help citizens catch preventable welfare-application mistakes *before* they submit their papers. Our AI reads the documents; a tested rule engine checks them; and Cline maintains the rules as official guidelines change.\n 4 | **Promise:** we reduce preventable errors. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## Problem (evidence: docs/research.md)\n 7 | Eligible people lose benefits after applying because their documents disagree (name spellings across Aadhaar, bank and land record; account not Aadhaar-seeded; missing papers) or because rejections arrive unexplained. In Rajasthan in 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the third instalment, mostly due to name mismatches with Aadhaar.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current using the Cline agent.\n12 | \n13 | ## Languages\n14 | **Assamese (default) + English toggle.** All fixed UI and check messages live in one `src/i18n.ts` with `as` and `en` keys. Assamese strings must be reviewed by a native speaker before the demo (Das will arrange). AI-generated Assamese (letters, explanations) is labelled \"draft\".\n15 | \n16 | ## Scope: rule packs v2 (docs/schemes.md is the source of truth)\n17 | - **PM-KISAN: flagship, full end-to-end demo** (name mismatch, missing document, uncertain bank status).\n18 | - **Orunodoi 3.0: Assam relevance, verified rules only;** provisional criteria → \"needs verification\".\n19 | - **Widow Pension (IGNWPS): simple, reliable rules** (age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month).\n20 | \n21 | ## Architecture (the trust design)\n22 | 1. **Document reader (AI):** extracts names, dates, account details and document type, with per-field confidence. Low confidence → user confirms.\n23 | 2. **Deterministic rule engine (pure code, tested):** normalises fields, checks consistency, evaluates verified criteria, finds missing documents. Provisional rules and external facts → `needs_verification`.\n24 | 3. **Two separate verdicts:** *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification).\n25 | 4. **Next steps:** corrections, where to go (bank, Aadhaar centre, circle office, Gram Panchayat), the source of each rule, and a printable cover sheet.\n26 | 5. **Explainer (AI, optional):** friendly wording in Assamese, built only from the engine's result.\n27 | \n28 | ## Core loop (must-ship demo path)\n29 | Pick scheme → add documents (photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm low-confidence fields → answer yes/no questions → two-verdict report with fixes and sources → print cover sheet.\n30 | Samples (clearly fake): A = clean PM-KISAN farmer → ready_for_review (+ bank seeding needs verification). B = PM-KISAN with \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" (bank, possible match) and \"Rameshwar Sharma\" (land record, mismatch) → action_required. C = widow pension, missing death certificate → action_required.\n31 | \n32 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n33 | Upload or paste a scheme notice → a `@cline/sdk` Agent proposes a **rule change** (new scheme or edited rule, with provenance: sourceUrl, clause, effectiveDate) → writes **regression tests** → runs them through the engine (existing scheme tests must still pass) → shows a diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme) and `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (a one-time payment change, to show versioning).\n34 | \n35 | ## Trust rules (non-negotiable)\n36 | - AI reads and explains; **code decides**. No eligibility claim from model text.\n37 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n38 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional → needs_verification.\n39 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity.\n40 | - Demo uses fake documents only.\n41 | \n42 | ## Data model sketch\n43 | - `RuleProvenance` { sourceUrl, sourceTitle, clause?, effectiveDate?, verifiedOn, version, status: verified | provisional }\n44 | - `SchemeRule` { id, version, nameEn, nameAs, benefit { centralShare, stateTopUp|null, period, effectiveDate, provenance }, mandatoryDocs[], supportingDocs[], ageRange?, eligibilityAnyOf[], exclusions[], externalChecks[], each criterion with provenance }\n45 | - `ExtractedDoc` { docType, fields { name, dob, aadhaarLast4, accountNo, ifsc, ownerNames[], husbandName, ... }, confidence per field }\n46 | - `Report` { eligibility, readiness, checks[], schemeVersion, asOfDate }\n47 | - DB (T3): `rule_versions` { schemeId, version, ruleJson, testsJson, testResultJson, status: proposed | published | rejected, sourceNote, createdAt, approvedAt }\n48 | \n49 | ## Stretch\n50 | Assamese voice readout (only if the browser has an as-IN voice; otherwise hide) · rejection-notice decoder (T4) · helper mode for many applicants.\n51 | \n52 | ## Cut list (cut in this order)\n53 | Voice → decoder letter drafting → real photo upload (keep samples + manual entry) → cover-sheet styling. **Never cut:** the two-verdict report, provenance, the Cline agent with tests + approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\productContext.md","result":" 1 | # Product context: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Why it exists\n 4 | Eligible people lose welfare benefits *after* applying: names that don't match across Aadhaar, bank and land records; Aadhaar not seeded to the bank; missing certificates; rejection reasons they cannot understand. Documented example: Rajasthan 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the 3rd instalment, mostly because of Aadhaar name mismatches (sources in `docs/research.md`).\n 5 | \n 6 | KaagazCheck checks the papers **before** the person applies, in **Assamese (default) with an English toggle**, and says exactly what to fix and where.\n 7 | **Promise:** we help catch preventable mistakes. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam (farmer, widow, woman of a household) on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current with the Rule Maintenance Agent (Cline SDK).\n12 | \n13 | ## Schemes in scope (rule packs v2, `docs/schemes.md` is the source of truth)\n14 | - **PM-KISAN** (`pm-kisan`): flagship end-to-end demo. No landholding-size limit.\n15 | - **Orunodoi 3.0, Assam** (`orunodoi-3`): only the ration card and ₹1,250/month are verified; everything else is provisional → \"needs verification\".\n16 | - **Widow Pension IGNWPS** (`nsap-widow`): age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month; state top-up unconfirmed.\n17 | \n18 | ## Main demo path (3 minutes)\n19 | 1. Pick a scheme.\n20 | 2. Add documents: photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\" (A clean PM-KISAN, B name mismatch, C widow missing death certificate).\n21 | 3. AI reads each document → fields + confidence; low confidence → the user confirms or edits.\n22 | 4. Answer the yes/no questions.\n23 | 5. Rule engine → **two verdicts**: *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification). Each check has a reason, where to fix it, and its source (provenance, verified vs provisional).\n24 | 6. Assamese report + printable cover sheet.\n25 | \n26 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n27 | A scheme notice → the agent proposes a rule change (new scheme or new version, with provenance) → writes regression tests → runs them through the engine → diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme), `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (one-time ₹1,500 for October 2026, via a time-bounded benefit override).\n28 | \n29 | ## Second mode (T4)\n30 | Rejection decoder: rejection text → known reason code (`src/core/rejectionCodes.ts`) → fix steps in Assamese + English.\n31 | \n32 | ## Trust rules\n33 | - The AI only reads and explains; the rule engine decides.\n34 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional rules and external facts (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) → needs_verification, never a definitive pass/fail.\n35 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity: only an exact (normalised) match is `ok`.\n36 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n37 | - Demo uses fake sample documents only. AI-generated Assamese is labelled \"draft\"; fixed Assamese strings need native-speaker review.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\systemPatterns.md","result":" 1 | # System patterns\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Core pipeline: AI reads → rule engine decides → AI explains\n 4 | 1. **Read (AI):** a document image or text → `ExtractedDoc` (fields + per-field confidence), validated with zod.\n 5 | 2. **Decide (pure code):** `evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report` in `src/core/evaluate.ts`. Deterministic, unit- and property-tested. No model text ever decides a status.\n 6 | 3. **Explain (AI, optional):** friendlier Assamese wording or a letter draft, built only from the report's checks (labelled \"draft\").\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Module boundaries\n 9 | - `src/core/`: pure TypeScript. No React, network, DB, `process.env` or implicit \"today\" (`asOfDate` is always passed in).\n10 |   - `types.ts` zod schemas: `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (versioned), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n11 |   - `schemes/` rule packs (`pm-kisan.ts`, `orunodoi-3.ts`, `nsap-widow.ts`; provenance helpers in `sources.ts`) + registry `index.ts`: `getScheme(id, version?)`, `listSchemes()`, `listSchemeVersions(id)`, `registerScheme(rule)` (validates; keeps old versions; newest wins), `questionsFor(scheme)`.\n12 |   - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`), `age.ts` (`ageOn`), `aadhaar.ts` (`maskAadhaar`), `benefit.ts` (`benefitOn` with time-bounded overrides), `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts` (bilingual doc/office labels, disclaimer), `samples.ts` (fake sample sets A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n13 |   - T2 UI helpers (pure, client-safe; they don't import the engine): `extraction.ts` (raw model JSON → `ExtractedDoc`), `docFields.ts`, `flow.ts`, `reportView.ts` (sections/tones/₹ formatting), `catalog.ts` (`SchemeView`), `thresholds.ts`.\n14 | - `src/i18n.ts` (T2): every fixed UI string in `as` + `en` (same keys, tested); reuses `labels.ts`.\n15 | - `src/server/ai.ts` (T2): the **only** module that calls a model. Structured JSON → zod → one retry → safe fallback `{ error }`. Logs model, prompt version, input hash (never raw personal data). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests.\n16 | - `src/server/api.ts` (T2): request schemas + handlers for `/api/check` (engine only) and `/api/extract` (via ai.ts); the route files are thin wrappers.\n17 | - `src/app/_components/` (T2): the single client flow `KaagazApp` and its steps; `page.tsx` (server) passes a plain catalog + samples.\n18 | - T3 pure core: `ruleTests.ts` (zod `RuleTestCase` benefit|evaluate + deterministic `runRuleTests`), `schemes/regression.ts` (built-in regression suites), `ruleDiff.ts` (keyed before/after diff), `ruleDiffView.ts` (plain-English labels for the UI), `rulePolicy.ts` (version bump, ≥ 3 new tests, verified-provenance rule), `mergePatch.ts` (RFC 7386), `notice.ts` (normalise; extract the demo notices), `agentLog.ts` (one-line tool summaries).\n19 | - `src/server/store.ts` (T3): the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL, every write in `BEGIN IMMEDIATE … COMMIT`); `rule_versions` table (+ `notice`, `summary`).\n20 | - `src/server/rules.ts` (T3): `RuleService`: candidate (full rule or merge patch) → validate (zod + policy) → runTests (new + regression) → saveProposal (only if all pass) → publish (re-check, then `registerScheme`) / reject. `syncRegistry()` loads published versions into the registry (idempotent; called per request).\n21 | - `src/server/agents/ruleMaintenance.ts` (T3): `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent: system prompt + 5 `createTool` tools (zod inputs, re-validated with `checked()`), session state, `runRuleAgent(notice)` → streams `AgentEvent`s; the result comes from what was saved through the tools, never from the agent's text.\n22 | - `src/server/ai.ts` also has `runToolAgent` (Cline SDK `Agent`, `openai-compatible` → Cline API): it is still the only module that talks to a model.\n23 | - `src/server/adminApi.ts` + `src/app/api/admin/rules/**` (T3): propose (NDJSON stream), list (history + diff), `[id]/publish`, `[id]/reject`. `src/app/admin/` is the maintainer UI.\n24 | - T4: `src/server/adminAuth.ts` (optional `ADMIN_PASSCODE` → `adminGuard(req)` in every `/api/admin/*` route); `src/core/decode.ts` (pure: `RawClassification`, `decodeResult`, `ASK_AT_OFFICE`, `redactForModel`); `ai.ts classifyRejection()`; `api.ts handleDecode` + `src/app/api/decode/route.ts`; `src/app/decode/` UI; `RuleStore.resetAll()` + `scripts/demo-reset.mjs`; registry `resetRegistry()` / `runtimeVersionKeys()` (used by `syncRegistry` after a reset); `src/guardrails.test.ts` (trust-rule audit).\n25 | - `src/app/api/**/route.ts`: thin handlers on the Node.js runtime (the default; an explicit `runtime` export breaks the build with `cacheComponents`).\n26 | - `src/app/**`: UI (Assamese default, English toggle; fixed strings in `src/i18n.ts`). Calls API routes, never the model.\n27 | \n28 | ## Result model (docs/schemes.md v2)\n29 | - Check result: `ok | action_required | needs_verification | not_applicable`; kind: `document | name | field | eligibility | external`. Every check has `messageEn`, `messageAs`, `fixWhere`, `provenance`, plus `match` for name checks.\n30 | - **Eligibility:** `not_eligible` only when a **verified** eligibility criterion failed; any provisional, unanswered or unreadable criterion → `needs_verification`; else `likely_eligible`.\n31 | - **Readiness:** any `action_required` (missing mandatory doc, name `mismatch`, bad IFSC/account format, failed verified criterion) → `action_required`; else any non-external `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence, provisional) → `needs_verification`; else `ready_for_review`. External checks (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified, ration card active) are always `needs_verification` and listed, but on their own they don't block `ready_for_review`.\n32 | - Money: `centralShare` + `stateTopUp` (null = unconfirmed → `total` null; never show an unconfirmed total). Overrides are inclusive date windows; the last matching one wins.\n33 | \n34 | ## Name matching (showcase, defensive)\n35 | Tokenise → drop leading honorifics (SHRI/SMT/MR/MRS/KUMARI/LATE…) → transliterate Devanagari/Assamese/Bengali → canonical variants (KR→KUMAR, MD/MOHD→MOHAMMAD, DEBI→DEVI, SK→SHEIKH…). Levels: `same` (identical after formatting; the only level that gives `ok`), `possible_match` (variants, transliteration, word order, or every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85), `initials_only`, `mismatch` (incl. a missing/extra word). The score is shown but never decides.\n36 | \n37 | ## Privacy\n38 | Aadhaar: only `aadhaarLast4` is stored in `ExtractedDoc`; `maskAadhaar` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`. Images processed in memory only. Minimum personal data.\n39 | \n40 | ## Testing\n41 | Vitest + fast-check, tests first for core logic. Properties: name same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never `ok`, Orunodoi never `not_eligible`, evaluate deterministic + schema-valid, readiness invariant.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\techContext.md","result":" 1 | # Tech context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Stack\n 4 | - One Next.js 16 app (App Router, `src/` dir, `@/*` → `./src/*`), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`).\n 5 | - Validation: zod 4.\n 6 | - Tests: Vitest 5 (Node environment, `src/**/*.test.ts`) + fast-check 4.\n 7 | - Lint: ESLint 9 flat config (`eslint-config-next`); `next lint` no longer exists in Next 16.\n 8 | - Database (T3, done): built-in `node:sqlite` (WAL, SQLite 3.53.4) in `src/server/store.ts`; no fallback needed.\n 9 | - AI: Cline API (OpenAI-compatible), base URL `https://api.cline.bot/api/v1`, all calls via `src/server/ai.ts`.\n10 | - In-product agent (T3, done): `@cline/sdk@0.0.92` `Agent`, `providerId: \"openai-compatible\"`, tools via `createTool` with zod schemas (details below).\n11 | \n12 | ## Environment\n13 | - Windows, PowerShell 5.1; the path contains a space (`C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build`). Use npm scripts and cross-platform Node code.\n14 | - Node v24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, git 2.55.0.\n15 | - Secrets only in `.env.local` (git-ignored): `CLINE_API_KEY`, `CLINE_MODEL` (e.g. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, never a `:batch` model). The template is `.env.example`.\n16 | - Write files containing Assamese (or other non-Latin text) with the editor tool (UTF-8), not PowerShell redirection. Assamese uses ৰ (U+09F0) and ৱ (U+09F1), not Bengali র/ব.\n17 | - The editor tool rejects payloads over ~6000 characters: write large files in chunks (create, then insert at the end).\n18 | - `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so never leave scratch `.ts` files in the repo root while running `next build`.\n19 | \n20 | ## npm scripts\n21 | | Script | Command |\n22 | |---|---|\n23 | | `dev` | `next dev` |\n24 | | `build` | `next build` |\n25 | | `start` | `next start` |\n26 | | `lint` | `eslint .` |\n27 | | `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |\n28 | | `test` | `vitest run` |\n29 | | `test:watch` | `vitest` |\n30 | | `demo:reset` | `node --env-file-if-exists=.env.local … scripts/demo-reset.mjs` (clears `rule_versions`) |\n31 | \n32 | ## Gotchas found in T4\n33 | - Node 24 runs `.ts` imports from a `.mjs` script directly (type stripping), but warns `MODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON`; the npm script passes `--disable-warning=MODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON`.\n34 | - The ESLint rule `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rejects calling a function that sets state inside `useEffect`; do the fetch inline in the effect with a `live` flag.\n35 | - Windows: an open `node:sqlite` file can't be removed by `rmSync` in a test's `afterEach`; close every `RuleStore` first.\n36 | - Smoke-testing with `next start`: if the shell has an empty `CLINE_MODEL`, set it from `.env.local` for the process (see T2) or the decoder answers `ai_unavailable`.\n37 | \n38 | ## Gotchas found in T0\n39 | - Vitest 5 needs `@types/node` ≥ 22 (peer dep), so `@types/node` is `^22`.\n40 | - The Vitest config is `vitest.config.mts` (ESM); a `.ts` config triggers a Vite \"configLoader native\" warning because `package.json` has no `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n41 | - The global `LayoutProps<\"/\">` type only exists after `next build`/`next dev` generate `.next/types`, so `layout.tsx` uses an explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` to keep `npm run typecheck` working on a clean checkout.\n42 | - Vite writes warnings to stderr, which PowerShell reports as `NativeCommandError`. Check the real exit code (e.g. run via `cmd /c ... & echo %ERRORLEVEL%`).\n43 | - `npm install` is slow here (about 5 minutes for a fresh install); long commands can exceed the tool timeout, so run them in the background with logs.\n44 | \n45 | ## Gotchas found in T2\n46 | - Next 16.4 + `cacheComponents: true` **rejects `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"`** in route files (build error). Node.js is the default runtime, so routes omit it.\n47 | - The Cline API (`/chat/completions`) returns the OpenAI body wrapped as `{ data: { choices: [...] } }`. Image input (`image_url` data URL) works with `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`.\n48 | - This PowerShell session had an **empty `CLINE_MODEL` env var** set. Next never overrides an existing env var from `.env.local`, so the AI looked unconfigured. Run `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL` before `next dev`/`next start` if `/api/extract` says `ai_unavailable` while `.env.local` is filled.\n49 | - In Vitest, `beforeEach(() => mock.mockReset())` returns the mock, which Vitest then runs as a teardown. Use a block body `beforeEach(() => { mock.mockReset(); })`.\n50 | - Manual smoke test: `npm run build`, `npx next start -p 3123`, `node scripts/smoke.mjs http://localhost:3123`.\n51 | \n52 | ## Cline SDK (`@cline/sdk` 0.0.92), found in T3 by reading node_modules\n53 | - `@cline/sdk` is only `export * from \"@cline/core\"`. Core re-exports `Agent` (from `@cline/agents`, same class as `AgentRuntime`) and `createTool` (from `@cline/shared`). ESM-only, Node ≥ 22, depends on zod ^4.\n54 | - `new Agent({ providerId: \"openai-compatible\", baseUrl: \"https://api.cline.bot/api/v1\", apiKey, modelId, systemPrompt, tools, maxIterations, toolExecution })` → `agent.run(text)` returns `{ status: \"completed\"|\"aborted\"|\"failed\", outputText, iterations, usage, error? }`. `agent.subscribe(fn)` streams events: `tool-started` / `tool-finished` (`toolCall { toolCallId, toolName, input }`, `message.content[].output`), `assistant-text-delta` (`accumulatedText`), `run-failed`, etc. `agent.abort()` cancels.\n55 | - `createTool({ name, description, inputSchema: zodSchema, execute })` converts zod → JSON Schema (`additionalProperties: false`). It does **not** zod-validate the input before `execute` (verified: `{a: 5}` reached a `z.string()` tool), so each tool wraps `execute` in `checked(schema, fn)` → `safeParse` → `{ error }`. Default tool timeout 30 s, retryable, max 3 retries.\n56 | - The agent retries transient provider errors itself. A thrown `execute` error becomes an `isError` tool result the model sees.\n57 | - Matches .clinerules/03-stack.md; no differences in the API used.\n58 | - **Turbopack cannot bundle `@cline/core`** (dynamic `new URL(\"./entry.\"+ext, import.meta.url)` worker URLs → 72 \"Module not found\" errors). Fixed with `serverExternalPackages: [\"@cline/sdk\", \"@cline/core\", \"@cline/agents\", \"@cline/llms\", \"@cline/shared\"]` in `next.config.ts`.\n59 | - `ai.ts` imports `@cline/sdk` lazily (dynamic import) inside the real agent factory; `ruleMaintenance.ts` imports `createTool` statically (cold import ≈ 1.4 s, only on admin routes).\n60 | - Live timing with `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`: Orunodoi notice ≈ 21 s (6 tool calls), IGNOAPS new scheme ≈ 30–60 s. Longer than the tool timeout here, so run `scripts/agent-smoke.mjs` in the background with a log.\n61 | \n62 | ## T3 storage\n63 | - `node:sqlite` works inside Next 16 route handlers and Vitest (no build trouble). DB file: `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH` or `data/kaagaz.db` (`/data/` is git-ignored). Vitest sets `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH=:memory:` (vitest.config.mts), so tests never touch `data/`.\n64 | - A page that reads the DB/registry per request needs `await connection()` inside a `<Suspense>` child (Cache Components). `connection()` throws outside a Next request scope, so unit tests call the handler (`handleList`) instead of the route.\n65 | - `cmd /c \"x & echo %ERRORLEVEL%\"` expands ERRORLEVEL too early (prints empty). Use `cmd /c \"npm test >nul 2>&1\"; $LASTEXITCODE` in PowerShell.\n66 | \n67 | ## Scaffold notes\n68 | Generated with `create-next-app@16.4.0` in a temp folder and copied in (it refuses non-empty folders). Defaults kept: `cacheComponents: true`, `partialPrefetching: true`. `AGENTS.md` is written by Next (`next dev` re-adds it), so it is committed.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\README.md","result":"1 | # Memory Bank\n2 | Empty until the problem statement is released. In task T0, Cline creates:\n3 | `projectbrief.md` (from Claude's brief), `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md`.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\README-draft.md","result":" 1 | # KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): Check before you apply\n 2 | \n 3 | > We help citizens catch preventable welfare-application mistakes **before** they submit their papers. AI reads the documents; a tested rule engine checks them; and a Cline agent maintains the rules as official guidelines change.\n 4 | >\n 5 | > We reduce preventable errors. We do **not** guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 6 | \n 7 | ## The problem\n 8 | Eligible people in India often lose welfare benefits *after* applying, because their documents disagree with each other (a name spelled differently on Aadhaar, the bank passbook and the land record; an account not linked to Aadhaar; a missing certificate), or because a rejection arrives with no reason they can understand.\n 9 | \n10 | - **Rajasthan, PM-KISAN (2019):** only about 23% of about 51 lakh registered farmers received the third instalment; officials cited names on applications not matching Aadhaar. ([Hindustan Times](https://www.pressreader.com/india/hindustan-times-st-jaipur/20191007/281586652343870))\n11 | - **Andhra Pradesh, PM-KISAN (LibTech India, 2022):** about 15.2 lakh farmers missed instalments and about ₹1,343 crore was pending; about half were held with \"action required by the state\" and no stated reason. ([LibTech report](https://libtech.in/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/‘PM-KISAN-Samman-Nidhi-AP-25th-January.pdf))\n12 | \n13 | Finding schemes is already served (myScheme, Jugalbandi). **Getting an application through without a preventable rejection is not.**\n14 | \n15 | ## The solution\n16 | A mobile web app in **Assamese (with English)**:\n17 | 1. Pick a scheme: **PM-KISAN** (flagship), **Orunodoi 3.0** (Assam), **Widow Pension (IGNWPS)**.\n18 | 2. Add documents: photo (AI reads them), type them in, or use fake demo samples.\n19 | 3. Confirm anything the AI was unsure about.\n20 | 4. Answer a few yes/no questions.\n21 | 5. Get **two separate verdicts**: *Eligibility* (likely eligible / not eligible / needs verification) and *Application readiness* (ready for review / action required / needs verification), each with what to fix, where to fix it (bank, Aadhaar centre, circle office, Gram Panchayat) and the official source of every rule.\n22 | 6. Print a cover sheet to carry to the office.\n23 | \n24 | Plus a **rejection decoder** (`/decode`): paste a rejection or status message and get the likely reason and fix steps.\n25 | \n26 | ## Cline inside the product: the Rule Maintenance Agent (`/admin`)\n27 | Government rules change. Paste a scheme notice and a **`@cline/sdk` agent**:\n28 | 1. reads the current rule pack and the notice;\n29 | 2. proposes the smallest rule change, with provenance (source, clause, effective date);\n30 | 3. writes regression tests and runs them **together with every existing test** for that scheme;\n31 | 4. shows a readable before/after diff and the test results;\n32 | 5. waits for a **human to Publish**; then the citizen app uses the new version immediately, and old versions are kept.\n33 | \n34 | The agent works only through five tools (`getRuleSchema`, `getCurrentRule`, `proposeRule`, `runTests`, `saveProposal`). **Code, not the prompt, enforces the safety rules:** the version must go up; at least 3 new tests; nothing marked \"verified\" without an official source; no save unless all tests pass; Publish re-runs every check.\n35 | \n36 | Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (adds the Old Age Pension) and `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (a one-time ₹1,500 payment for October 2026, with ₹1,250 still the regular amount).\n37 | \n38 | ## Architecture\n39 | ```\n40 | Phone browser ──► Next.js app (App Router)\n41 |                    ├─ / (citizen flow)     ├─ /decode       ├─ /admin (rule maintenance)\n42 |                    └─ API routes: /api/extract  /api/check  /api/decode  /api/admin/rules/*\n43 |                          │            │                         │\n44 |                  src/server/ai.ts   src/core/evaluate.ts   src/server/agents/ruleMaintenance.ts\n45 |                  (ONLY model caller; (pure, tested rule      (@cline/sdk Agent + 5 tools)\n46 |                   zod-validated JSON) engine: two verdicts,          │\n47 |                          │            provenance, name match)  src/server/store.ts\n48 |                  Cline API (OpenAI-                            (only DB writer, node:sqlite,\n49 |                  compatible, vision)                            versioned rule packs)\n50 | ```\n51 | **Trust design:** the AI reads and explains; **code decides**. Provisional rules and facts a photo can't prove (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) always return \"needs verification\". A fuzzy name score never counts as a match; only names identical after formatting clean-up do. Aadhaar is masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images are processed in memory and never stored.\n52 | \n53 | ## Tech stack\n54 | Next.js 16 (App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind v4) · zod · Vitest + fast-check (property tests) · `node:sqlite` · `@cline/sdk` · Cline API (OpenAI-compatible) for vision and language.\n55 | \n56 | ## Setup\n57 | ```bash\n58 | npm install\n59 | cp .env.example .env.local    # then fill in CLINE_API_KEY and CLINE_MODEL (optional: ADMIN_PASSCODE)\n60 | npm run dev                   # http://localhost:3000  ·  /admin  ·  /decode\n61 | npm test                      # unit + property tests\n62 | npm run demo:reset            # restore the original 3 rule packs before a demo\n63 | ```\n64 | Windows note: if the app says \"AI unavailable\" although `.env.local` is filled in, run `Remove-Item Env:CLINE_MODEL` in that terminal (an empty shell variable overrides the file).\n65 | \n66 | ## How we used Cline\n67 | **Workflow:** Claude (in Claude Desktop) acted as architect and reviewer; **Cline wrote the code**. Claude wrote specs only (`docs/`, `memory-bank/projectbrief.md`, `tasks/`); Cline built every task through a local bridge that runs the official Cline CLI, and every run is logged in `.cline-runs/`.\n68 | \n69 | | Task | Cline run | What Cline built |\n70 | |---|---|---|\n71 | | T0 plan | `run-133031-4cma` (Plan mode) | Setup plan with Windows risks (path with a space, Devanagari encoding) |\n72 | | T0 | `run-133358-c1ef` | Next.js scaffold, Vitest, Memory Bank, first commit |\n73 | | T1 | `run-134715-f3yl` | Rule engine v2 with tests first: name matching, two verdicts, provenance (93 tests) |\n74 | | T2 | `run-144641-b8cr` | Assamese mobile flow, AI document reader, API routes (150 tests) |\n75 | | T3 | `run-152706-g9km` | `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent, versioned store, /admin (225 tests) |\n76 | | T4 | *(fill in)* | Admin passcode, guardrails audit, rejection decoder, demo reset |\n77 | \n78 | **Cline features used:** Plan/Act modes · `.clinerules/` (quality, workflow, stack rules) · Memory Bank (`memory-bank/`) · task specs (`tasks/NEXT.md`, `tasks/backlog/`) · the run log in `tasks/LOG.md` · the Cline CLI driven headlessly · **`@cline/sdk` inside the product**.\n79 | \n80 | **Honest attribution:** product research, the problem framing and the rule-pack research were done by Das with Claude; corrections to the rule packs came from Das's review against government sources. *(If any code was written outside Cline, list it here.)*\n81 | \n82 | ## Limitations and future scope\n83 | - Rule packs cover 3 schemes; Orunodoi 3.0 exclusions are provisional until a current official guideline is confirmed.\n84 | - Payment bands by age (e.g. ₹500 at 80+ for old age pension) aren't modelled yet.\n85 | - Assamese text needs a native-speaker review; voice output is future work.\n86 | - Next: helper mode for CSC/NGO workers handling many applicants, an official status lookup where APIs exist, more states and languages.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\README.md","result":" 1 | # KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\n 2 | \n 3 | The government checks your papers after you apply and rejects you months later. KaagazCheck checks them **before** you apply, in Hindi, and tells you exactly what to fix.\n 4 | \n 5 | > Work in progress (Cline AI Builder Hackathon). The full README (problem, architecture, how Cline was used) comes in the final task.\n 6 | \n 7 | ## Setup\n 8 | Requires Node 22+.\n 9 | \n10 | ```powershell\n11 | npm install\n12 | copy .env.example .env.local   # then fill in CLINE_API_KEY and CLINE_MODEL\n13 | npm run dev\n14 | ```\n15 | \n16 | ## Scripts\n17 | `npm test` · `npm run typecheck` · `npm run lint` · `npm run build`","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\.env.example","result":"1 | CLINE_API_KEY=\n2 | CLINE_MODEL=\n3 | # Optional: where published rule versions are stored (default data/kaagaz.db, git-ignored)\n4 | KAAGAZ_DB_PATH=\n5 | # Optional: passcode for /admin and /api/admin/* (header x-admin-passcode). Empty = unprotected demo mode.\n6 | ADMIN_PASSCODE=","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\package.json","result":" 1 | {\n 2 |   \"name\": \"kaagazcheck\",\n 3 |   \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n 4 |   \"private\": true,\n 5 |   \"engines\": {\n 6 |     \"node\": \">=22\"\n 7 |   },\n 8 |   \"scripts\": {\n 9 |     \"dev\": \"next dev\",\n10 |     \"build\": \"next build\",\n11 |     \"start\": \"next start\",\n12 |     \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n13 |     \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n14 |     \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n15 |     \"test:watch\": \"vitest\",\n16 |     \"demo:reset\": \"node --env-file-if-exists=.env.local --disable-warning=MODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON scripts/demo-reset.mjs\"\n17 |   },\n18 |   \"dependencies\": {\n19 |     \"@cline/sdk\": \"^0.0.92\",\n20 |     \"next\": \"16.4.0\",\n21 |     \"react\": \"19.3.0\",\n22 |     \"react-dom\": \"19.3.0\",\n23 |     \"zod\": \"^4.6.5\"\n24 |   },\n25 |   \"devDependencies\": {\n26 |     \"@tailwindcss/turbopack\": \"^4\",\n27 |     \"@types/node\": \"^22.20.5\",\n28 |     \"@types/react\": \"^19\",\n29 |     \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19\",\n30 |     \"eslint\": \"^9\",\n31 |     \"eslint-config-next\": \"16.4.0\",\n32 |     \"fast-check\": \"^4.10.2\",\n33 |     \"tailwindcss\": \"^4\",\n34 |     \"typescript\": \"^5\",\n35 |     \"vitest\": \"^5.0.3\"\n36 |   }\n37 | }","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\.gitignore","result":" 1 | # See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.\n 2 | \n 3 | # dependencies\n 4 | /node_modules\n 5 | /.pnp\n 6 | .pnp.*\n 7 | .yarn/*\n 8 | !.yarn/patches\n 9 | !.yarn/plugins\n10 | !.yarn/releases\n11 | !.yarn/versions\n12 | \n13 | # testing\n14 | /coverage\n15 | \n16 | # next.js\n17 | /.next/\n18 | /out/\n19 | \n20 | # production\n21 | /build\n22 | \n23 | # misc\n24 | .DS_Store\n25 | *.pem\n26 | \n27 | # debug\n28 | npm-debug.log*\n29 | yarn-debug.log*\n30 | yarn-error.log*\n31 | .pnpm-debug.log*\n32 | \n33 | # env files: secrets stay local; .env.example IS committed\n34 | .env\n35 | .env.local\n36 | .env*.local\n37 | !.env.example\n38 | \n39 | # vercel\n40 | .vercel\n41 | \n42 | # typescript\n43 | *.tsbuildinfo\n44 | next-env.d.ts\n45 | \n46 | # local databases (node:sqlite) and the app's data folder\n47 | /data/\n48 | *.db\n49 | *.db-wal\n50 | *.db-shm\n51 | \n52 | # NOTE: .cline-runs/ is intentionally NOT ignored (evidence of Cline runs)","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\src\\server\\agents\\ruleMaintenance.ts","result":"  1 | // The Rule Maintenance Agent: a @cline/sdk Agent that turns a scheme notice into a proposed,\n  2 | // tested rule-pack version. It acts ONLY through these five tools (zod inputs); it never writes\n  3 | // files and never publishes. Every check (schema, policy, tests) is code; a person approves.\n  4 | import { createTool } from \"@cline/sdk\";\n  5 | import { z } from \"zod\";\n  6 | import { summarizeToolInput, summarizeToolOutput } from \"@/core/agentLog\";\n  7 | import { normalizeNotice } from \"@/core/notice\";\n  8 | import { diffRules, type RuleChange } from \"@/core/ruleDiff\";\n  9 | import { MIN_NEW_TESTS } from \"@/core/rulePolicy\";\n 10 | import { RuleTestCase, type TestReport } from \"@/core/ruleTests\";\n 11 | import { listSchemes } from \"@/core/schemes\";\n 12 | import { SchemeRule } from \"@/core/types\";\n 13 | import { runToolAgent, type ToolAgentDeps } from \"../ai\";\n 14 | import { getRuleService, type RuleService } from \"../rules\";\n 15 | import type { RuleVersionStatus } from \"../store\";\n 16 | \n 17 | export const RULE_AGENT_PROMPT_VERSION = \"rule-agent-v1\";\n 18 | \n 19 | export const SYSTEM_PROMPT = `You maintain the rule packs of KaagazCheck, a welfare-application checker for Assam, India.\n 20 | You receive the text of an official scheme notice or guideline. Turn it into a proposed rule-pack version, tested, for a human to approve.\n 21 | You can act ONLY through your tools. You cannot edit files, and you cannot publish: a person reviews and publishes.\n 22 | \n 23 | Steps:\n 24 | 1. Call getRuleSchema once to see the rule format, one example, and the existing schemes.\n 25 | 2. Decide: is this a change to an existing scheme, or a new scheme? If it changes one, call getCurrentRule(schemeId) to see the live rule and its regression tests.\n 26 | 3. Call proposeRule with the SMALLEST change that matches the notice:\n 27 |    - Existing scheme: pass { schemeId, patch } where patch is a JSON merge patch on the current rule (objects merge, arrays are replaced whole, null deletes). Bump version (e.g. 2.0.0 → 2.1.0).\n 28 |    - New scheme: pass { rule } with a full rule; a new kebab-case id; version \"1.0.0\".\n 29 |    - A temporary payment change is a benefit override (from/to dates, amount), not a change to the regular amount.\n 30 | 4. Call runTests with at least ${MIN_NEW_TESTS} NEW test cases for what the notice says (amounts on dates inside and outside any window, eligibility edges such as ages just inside and outside a limit, a missing required document). Existing regression tests run automatically and must keep passing. If something fails, fix the rule or a wrong test and run again.\n 31 | 5. When proposeRule is valid and every test passes, call saveProposal once with the same tests, a one-line sourceNote, and a short plain-English summary for the reviewer.\n 32 | \n 33 | Rules:\n 34 | - Never invent criteria, amounts, documents or dates that are not in the notice. If something is unclear or missing, leave it out and say so in a scheme note (notes) and in the summary.\n 35 | - Provenance on every rule you add or change: sourceTitle, clause (quote or paraphrase the notice), effectiveDate if stated, verifiedOn = today's date given below, version = the new version.\n 36 |   status \"verified\" ONLY with an official sourceUrl that appears in the notice text; otherwise status \"provisional\" with sourceUrl null (or the notice's URL if it is not official). Keep untouched provenance as it is.\n 37 | - Write Assamese (…As fields) in Assamese script (use ৰ and ৱ); it will be reviewed by a native speaker.\n 38 | - Use only these document types, places and fields from the schema. Keep test ids short, lowercase, unique, not reusing regression test ids.\n 39 | - Do not paste the whole rule back when a patch will do. Be concise in your final message (one or two sentences).`;\n 40 | \n 41 | export interface AgentSession {\n 42 |   notice: string;\n 43 |   /** The last rule that passed proposeRule (schema + policy). */\n 44 |   candidate: SchemeRule | null;\n 45 |   /** The live version it changes, or null for a new scheme. */\n 46 |   previous: SchemeRule | null;\n 47 |   savedId: number | null;\n 48 | }\n 49 | \n 50 | export function newSession(notice: string): AgentSession {\n 51 |   return { notice, candidate: null, previous: null, savedId: null };\n 52 | }\n 53 | \n 54 | function exampleRule() {\n 55 |   // The widow pension is the smallest complete built-in rule; its shape is the best example.\n 56 |   return listSchemes().find((s) => s.id === \"nsap-widow\");\n 57 | }\n 58 | \n 59 | const ProposeInput = z.object({\n 60 |   schemeId: z.string().max(64).optional().describe(\"Existing scheme id when sending a patch.\"),\n 61 |   patch: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional().describe(\"JSON merge patch on the current rule of schemeId.\"),\n 62 |   rule: z.record(z.string(), z.unknown()).optional().describe(\"A full SchemeRule (for a new scheme).\"),\n 63 | });\n 64 | \n 65 | const TestsInput = z.object({\n 66 |   tests: z.array(z.record(z.string(), z.unknown())).min(1).max(30).describe(\"Test cases (see testCase in getRuleSchema).\"),\n 67 | });\n 68 | \n 69 | const SaveInput = TestsInput.extend({\n 70 |   sourceNote: z.string().min(1).max(300).describe(\"Where the change comes from, in one line.\"),\n 71 |   summary: z.string().min(1).max(1000).describe(\"Plain-English summary of the change for the reviewer.\"),\n 72 | });\n 73 | \n 74 | /**\n 75 |  * `createTool` passes the model's raw input to `execute` without checking it, so every tool\n 76 |  * re-validates with its own zod schema and returns `{ error }` (seen by the model) instead of throwing.\n 77 |  */\n 78 | function checked<S extends z.ZodType, R>(schema: S, fn: (input: z.infer<S>) => Promise<R>) {\n 79 |   return async (input: unknown): Promise<R | { error: string }> => {\n 80 |     const parsed = schema.safeParse(input);\n 81 |     if (!parsed.success) {\n 82 |       const why = parsed.error.issues.slice(0, 5).map((i) => `${i.path.join(\".\") || \"(input)\"}: ${i.message}`);\n 83 |       return { error: `invalid input: ${why.join(\"; \")}` };\n 84 |     }\n 85 |     return fn(parsed.data);\n 86 |   };\n 87 | }\n 88 | \n 89 | /** The five tools. They share `session`, so runTests/saveProposal use the last valid proposal. */\n 90 | export function createRuleTools(service: RuleService, session: AgentSession) {\n 91 |   const getRuleSchema = createTool({\n 92 |     name: \"getRuleSchema\",\n 93 |     description: \"The SchemeRule JSON schema, the test-case JSON schema, one complete example rule, and the existing schemes.\",\n 94 |     inputSchema: z.object({}),\n 95 |     execute: async () => ({\n 96 |       schemeRule: z.toJSONSchema(SchemeRule, { io: \"input\", unrepresentable: \"any\" }),\n 97 |       testCase: z.toJSONSchema(RuleTestCase, { io: \"input\", unrepresentable: \"any\" }),\n 98 |       example: exampleRule(),\n 99 |       schemes: listSchemes().map((s) => ({ id: s.id, version: s.version, nameEn: s.nameEn })),\n100 |       today: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10),\n101 |     }),\n102 |   });\n103 | \n104 |   const CurrentInput = z.object({ schemeId: z.string().min(1).max(64) });\n105 |   const getCurrentRule = createTool({\n106 |     name: \"getCurrentRule\",\n107 |     description: \"The current published rule of a scheme and the regression tests every new version must still pass.\",\n108 |     inputSchema: CurrentInput,\n109 |     execute: checked(CurrentInput, async ({ schemeId }) => {\n110 |       const rule = service.currentRule(schemeId);\n111 |       if (!rule) return { found: false, schemeId, note: \"No such scheme: propose a full rule to add it.\" };\n112 |       return { found: true, rule, regressionTests: service.regressionTests(schemeId) };\n113 |     }),\n114 |   });\n115 | \n116 |   const proposeRule = createTool({\n117 |     name: \"proposeRule\",\n118 |     description:\n119 |       \"Validate a proposed rule (schema + policy). Pass {schemeId, patch} to change an existing scheme, or {rule} for a new one. Returns the problems, or valid + the list of changes.\",\n120 |     inputSchema: ProposeInput,\n121 |     execute: checked(ProposeInput, async (input) => {\n122 |       const cand = service.candidate(input);\n123 |       if (!cand.ok) return { valid: false, errors: cand.errors };\n124 |       const res = service.validate(cand.value, session.notice);\n125 |       if (!res.ok) return { valid: false, errors: res.errors };\n126 |       session.candidate = res.rule;\n127 |       session.previous = res.current;\n128 |       const changes = diffRules(res.current, res.rule);\n129 |       return { valid: true, schemeId: res.rule.id, version: res.rule.version, isNewScheme: res.current === null, changes: changes.slice(0, 40) };\n130 |     }),\n131 |   });\n132 | \n133 |   const runTests = createTool({\n134 |     name: \"runTests\",\n135 |     description: \"Run your new test cases AND all regression tests of the scheme against the last valid proposal, through the real rule engine.\",\n136 |     inputSchema: TestsInput,\n137 |     execute: checked(TestsInput, async ({ tests }) => {\n138 |       if (!session.candidate) return { ok: false, errors: [\"call proposeRule first (with a valid rule)\"] };\n139 |       const res = service.runTests(session.candidate, tests);\n140 |       if (!res.ok) return { ok: false, errors: res.errors };\n141 |       const { total, passed, failed } = res.report;\n142 |       return { ok: true, total, passed, failed, results: res.report.results };\n143 |     }),\n144 |   });\n145 | \n146 |   const saveProposal = createTool({\n147 |     name: \"saveProposal\",\n148 |     description: \"Store the last valid proposal with its tests as 'proposed' for a person to review. Refused unless every test passes. Call once.\",\n149 |     inputSchema: SaveInput,\n150 |     execute: checked(SaveInput, async ({ tests, sourceNote, summary }) => {\n151 |       if (session.savedId !== null) return { saved: false, errors: [`already saved as proposal #${session.savedId}`] };\n152 |       if (!session.candidate) return { saved: false, errors: [\"call proposeRule first (with a valid rule)\"] };\n153 |       const res = service.saveProposal({ rule: session.candidate, tests, sourceNote, summary, notice: session.notice });\n154 |       if (!res.ok) return { saved: false, errors: res.errors };\n155 |       session.savedId = res.row.id;\n156 |       return { saved: true, id: res.row.id, schemeId: res.row.schemeId, version: res.row.version, status: res.row.status };\n157 |     }),\n158 |   });\n159 | \n160 |   return [getRuleSchema, getCurrentRule, proposeRule, runTests, saveProposal];\n161 | }\n162 | \n163 | // ---------- the run ----------\n164 | \n165 | export interface ProposalView {\n166 |   id: number;\n167 |   schemeId: string;\n168 |   version: string;\n169 |   previousVersion: string | null;\n170 |   nameEn: string;\n171 |   status: RuleVersionStatus;\n172 |   sourceNote: string;\n173 |   summary: string;\n174 |   createdAt: string;\n175 |   approvedAt: string | null;\n176 |   changes: RuleChange[];\n177 |   testResult: TestReport;\n178 | }\n179 | \n180 | /** What the admin UI shows for one stored version: diff against the version before it. */\n181 | export function proposalView(row: { id: number; schemeId: string; version: string; rule: SchemeRule; status: RuleVersionStatus; sourceNote: string; summary: string; createdAt: string; approvedAt: string | null; testResult: TestReport }, previous: SchemeRule | null): ProposalView {\n182 |   return {\n183 |     id: row.id,\n184 |     schemeId: row.schemeId,\n185 |     version: row.version,\n186 |     previousVersion: previous?.version ?? null,\n187 |     nameEn: row.rule.nameEn,\n188 |     status: row.status,\n189 |     sourceNote: row.sourceNote,\n190 |     summary: row.summary,\n191 |     createdAt: row.createdAt,\n192 |     approvedAt: row.approvedAt,\n193 |     changes: diffRules(previous, row.rule),\n194 |     testResult: row.testResult,\n195 |   };\n196 | }\n197 | \n198 | export type AgentEvent =\n199 |   | { type: \"status\"; message: string }\n200 |   | { type: \"tool\"; id: string; name: string; phase: \"started\" | \"finished\"; summary: string; isError?: boolean }\n201 |   | { type: \"text\"; text: string }\n202 |   | { type: \"done\"; result: AgentRunResult };\n203 | \n204 | export type AgentRunResult =\n205 |   | { ok: true; proposal: ProposalView; agentText: string }\n206 |   | { ok: false; error: \"empty_notice\" | \"ai_unavailable\" | \"ai_failed\" | \"no_proposal\"; message: string; agentText?: string };\n207 | \n208 | \n209 | const RESULT_MESSAGES = {\n210 |   empty_notice: \"Paste the notice text first.\",\n211 |   ai_unavailable: \"The AI is not configured (CLINE_API_KEY / CLINE_MODEL). Nothing was changed.\",\n212 |   ai_failed: \"The agent could not finish. Nothing was published; try again.\",\n213 |   no_proposal: \"The agent finished without saving a valid, fully tested proposal. Nothing was published.\",\n214 | } as const;\n215 | \n216 | type ToolEvent = { type: string; toolCall?: { toolCallId?: string; toolName?: string; input?: unknown }; message?: { content?: { type?: string; output?: unknown; isError?: boolean }[] }; accumulatedText?: string };\n217 | \n218 | /** Turns raw SDK events into short UI events (tool name + one-line summary). */\n219 | function toAgentEvent(e: ToolEvent): AgentEvent | null {\n220 |   const call = e.toolCall;\n221 |   if (e.type === \"tool-started\" && call?.toolName) {\n222 |     return { type: \"tool\", id: call.toolCallId ?? \"\", name: call.toolName, phase: \"started\", summary: summarizeToolInput(call.toolName, call.input) };\n223 |   }\n224 |   if (e.type === \"tool-finished\" && call?.toolName) {\n225 |     const part = e.message?.content?.find((p) => p.type === \"tool-result\");\n226 |     const output = part?.output;\n227 |     const failed = part?.isError === true || (typeof output === \"object\" && output !== null && [\"valid\", \"ok\", \"saved\"].some((k) => (output as Record<string, unknown>)[k] === false));\n228 |     return { type: \"tool\", id: call.toolCallId ?? \"\", name: call.toolName, phase: \"finished\", summary: summarizeToolOutput(call.toolName, output), isError: failed };\n229 |   }\n230 |   return null;\n231 | }\n232 | \n233 | export interface RunOptions {\n234 |   service?: RuleService;\n235 |   onEvent?: (event: AgentEvent) => void;\n236 |   signal?: AbortSignal;\n237 |   aiDeps?: ToolAgentDeps;\n238 | }\n239 | \n240 | /** Runs the agent on a notice. The result is decided by what was saved through the tools, not by the agent's text. */\n241 | export async function runRuleAgent(noticeText: string, opts: RunOptions = {}): Promise<AgentRunResult> {\n242 |   const emit = opts.onEvent ?? (() => undefined);\n243 |   const finish = (result: AgentRunResult) => {\n244 |     emit({ type: \"done\", result });\n245 |     return result;\n246 |   };\n247 |   const notice = normalizeNotice(noticeText);\n248 |   if (!notice) return finish({ ok: false, error: \"empty_notice\", message: RESULT_MESSAGES.empty_notice });\n249 | \n250 |   const service = opts.service ?? getRuleService();\n251 |   const session = newSession(notice);\n252 |   const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n253 |   emit({ type: \"status\", message: \"Agent started\" });\n254 | \n255 |   let lastText = \"\";\n256 |   const run = await runToolAgent({\n257 |     promptVersion: RULE_AGENT_PROMPT_VERSION,\n258 |     systemPrompt: `${SYSTEM_PROMPT}\\n\\nToday's date: ${today}.`,\n259 |     input: `Scheme notice:\\n\"\"\"\\n${notice}\\n\"\"\"`,\n260 |     tools: createRuleTools(service, session),\n261 |     maxIterations: 16,\n262 |     signal: opts.signal,\n263 |     deps: opts.aiDeps,\n264 |     onEvent: (raw) => {\n265 |       const e = raw as ToolEvent;\n266 |       if (e.type === \"assistant-text-delta\" && typeof e.accumulatedText === \"string\") lastText = e.accumulatedText;\n267 |       const ev = toAgentEvent(e);\n268 |       if (ev) emit(ev);\n269 |     },\n270 |   });\n271 |   if (lastText) emit({ type: \"text\", text: lastText.slice(0, 2000) });\n272 | \n273 |   // Even if the run ended badly, a proposal saved through the tools is valid and fully tested.\n274 |   const row = session.savedId !== null ? service.get(session.savedId) : undefined;\n275 |   if (row) return finish({ ok: true, proposal: proposalView(row, session.previous), agentText: lastText });\n276 |   if (\"error\" in run) return finish({ ok: false, error: run.error, message: RESULT_MESSAGES[run.error], agentText: lastText });\n277 |   return finish({ ok: false, error: \"no_proposal\", message: RESULT_MESSAGES.no_proposal, agentText: run.outputText || lastText });\n278 | }\n279 | ","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\backlog\\T-last-freeze.md","result":"1 | # T-last — Freeze, red-team, demo (last 75 minutes)\n2 | \n3 | 1. No new features. Fix bugs only.\n4 | 2. `README.md`: the problem (3 lines), the solution, how to run, an architecture sketch, and **\"How we used Cline\"**: Plan/Act, .clinerules, Memory Bank, checkpoints, Cline CLI runs driven from Claude (logs in `.cline-runs/`), and the Cline SDK agent inside the product.\n5 | 3. `npm run demo:reset` — resets and seeds demo data.\n6 | 4. Final `npm test` + `npm run build`, commit, `git tag round2-final`.","success":true}],"durationMs":9}}
