{"ts":"2026-10-10T12:02:00.497Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_update","contentType":"tool","toolName":"run_commands","toolCallId":"toolu_01GBErfL9Dzi7TJEFSi8qEwQ","update":{"stream":"stdout","chunk":"- **Live agent check** (`scripts/agent-smoke.mjs --publish`, real Cline API, `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, throwaway DB):\r\n  - IGNOAPS notice â†’ new scheme `nsap-old-age` 1.0.0 in about 58 s (the first attempt timed out after 2 tool calls and the gateway retried). 11 top-level fields added; **5/5 new tests pass** (â‚¹200 central, age 60 ok, age 59 â†’ needs verification (provisional), missing BPL proof â†’ action required, age 85 ok). All provenance is provisional (Vikaspedia is not an official URL). The agent itself flagged that â‚¹500 for 80+ is only a note and that the upper age limit and office are placeholders.\r\n  - Orunodoi notice â†’ `orunodoi-3` 2.0.0 â†’ **2.1.0** in about 21 s. Changes: `version` + `benefit.overrides[0]` (2026-10-01 to 2026-10-31, stateTopUp 1500, provisional, sourceUrl null). **4 new + 4 regression tests pass**.\r\n  - After Publish: `/api/check` orunodoi-3 on 2026-10-15 â†’ 2.1.0, stateTopUp 1500, override true; on 2026-11-15 â†’ 1250, override false. `nsap-old-age` â†’ 200 central. The home page lists the Old Age Pension; `/admin` shows live 2.1.0 / 1.0.0 and the built-in versions in the history.\r\n\r\n**Design decisions / deviations (please review)**\r\n- **`rule_versions` has two extra columns, `notice` and `summary`.** `publish` re-checks the proposal, and the \"verified needs a URL from the notice\" rule needs the notice text; the summary is what the reviewer reads first.\r\n- **Proposal policy is code, not prompt:** the version must go up; â‰¥ 3 new tests; `verified` is allowed only if carried over unchanged or if its `sourceUrl` is in the notice. `saveProposal` is refused unless every test passes, and `publish` re-runs everything (so a second proposal for the same version can't go live after the first).\r\n- **Regression tests** = built-in suites + the tests of every published version, so the October tests protect the next Orunodoi version too.\r\n- **Merge patch for existing schemes** instead of the whole rule: fewer tokens, faster runs, a smaller chance of the model changing something by accident. New schemes are sent as a full rule.\r\n- **`createTool` does not validate input** (verified), so each tool `safeParse`s its input and returns `{ error }` to the model.\r\n- `runToolAgent` lives in `ai.ts` to keep rule 3 (one model module). It retries once **only if no tool has run**, because a second run after tool calls could repeat side effects.\r\n- `/admin` is English (maintainers, not citizens); the agent's Assamese strings are drafts.\r\n- The UI shows the IGNOAPS \"new scheme\" diff as one entry per top-level field (11 entries); nested detail is in the formatted values.\r\n\r\n**Open issues**\r\n- **`/admin` has no authentication.** Anyone who can reach the server can run the agent (it costs API credits) and publish rules. Fine for the local demo; must be decided before any deployment.\r\n- The engine supports one flat benefit amount, so IGNOAPS's â‚¹500 for 80+ is a note, not computed. The agent also used 120 as an upper age placeholder, because `AgeRange.max` is required.\r\n- A live run takes about 20â€“60 s; a model timeout can cost one retry (seen once in the IGNOAPS run).\r\n- I did not click through `/admin` or `/` in a real browser here (no browser automation). Both were checked through the server-rendered HTML and the APIs on `next start`.\r\n- `tasks/NEXT.md`, `.cline-runs/index.md` and `.cline-runs/run-144641-b8cr.log` were already modified before this run. I committed them as they are with `git add -A`, per the workflow, and did not edit them.\r\n\r\n**Requests for Claude**\r\n- Decide on `/admin` protection for the demo (e.g. a shared passcode in `.env.local`, or local-only), or confirm none.\r\n- Should the engine support age-banded benefits (IGNOAPS â‚¹200 for 60â€“79, â‚¹500 for 80+), and should `AgeRange.max` become optional (IGNOAPS has no upper limit)? Both are small schema/engine changes outside T3's scope.\r\n- Please confirm the two extra `rule_versions` columns (`notice`, `summary`).\r\n\r\n\r\n## T4 (trimmed): guardrails, admin passcode, decoder, demo reset (run-165739-gi16, 2026-10-10)\r\nFollowed `tasks/NEXT.md` in order (items 1â€“4 done; item 5 only the loading state on `/`). About 35 minutes.\r\n\r\n**1. Admin passcode**\r\n- `src/server/adminAuth.ts`: optional `ADMIN_PASSCODE`. When it's set, all 4 `/api/admin/*` routes need the header `x-admin-passcode` (constant-time compare). Otherwise they return 401 `{ error: \"passcode_required\" }`, which never echoes the passcode. Unset or blank means open.\r\n- `/admin`: when protected, the server sends no history and the page shows a passcode box. The passcode is kept in sessionStorage (`src/app/admin/passcode.ts`, `useSyncExternalStore`), sent on every admin fetch, and cleared on a 401. There is also a \"Lock\" button. When unprotected, the page shows an amber **\"Demo mode: unprotected\"** banner. `.env.example` now has `ADMIN_PASSCODE=`.\r\n- Tests: `src/server/adminAuth.test.ts` (4: pure checks + the real route handlers with the env var set; the agent never runs without the passcode).\r\n\r\n**2. Guardrails audit** (`src/guardrails.test.ts`, 14 tests, plus the existing tests listed below)\r\n| Guardrail | Result | Evidence |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Aadhaar masked in UI | âœ… | `ExtractedDoc.aadhaarLast4` must be exactly 4 digits (12-digit values are rejected); the confirm field has maxLength 4; `extraction.test.ts` property: a 12-digit Aadhaar never survives. |\r\n| â€¦ in logs | âœ… | Only `ai.ts` logs, through typed `AiLogEntry` (model, promptVersion, inputHash, outcome). `ai.test.ts` and `classify.test.ts` check that no name, digits or key appear. The decoder also masks 12-digit runs to the last 4 and other 9+ digit runs to `[number]` **before** sending to the model (`redactForModel`, property-tested). |\r\n| â€¦ in print | âœ… | The cover sheet is rendered in the test: `XXXX XXXX 4821`, no 12-digit run, no account number. |\r\n| No images stored | âœ… | No app code writes files; browser storage is only used for the admin passcode; only `store.ts` opens SQLite; its one table (`rule_versions`) has no image/photo/Aadhaar column. |\r\n| All AI output zod-validated | âœ… | Only `ai.ts` calls a model; `RawExtraction.safeParse` and `RawClassification.safeParse` run on every reply; agent tools re-validate their input (`checked()`). |\r\n| Disclaimer footer on every report | âœ… | `ReportStep` and `CoverSheet` are rendered for samples A/B/C in both languages, each with a `<footer>` holding both disclaimers. Property: every engine report carries them. `/decode` has its own bilingual disclaimer footer. |\r\n| Provenance + \"verified on\" + provisional badge on every check | âœ… (1 fix) | `CheckItem` is rendered for every check in A/B/C Ã— as/en: it shows the source title (link or \"no official link yet\"), \"verified on\", and the badge exactly when provisional. **Fixed:** the printed cover sheet only showed \"(provisional)\", so it now prints \"Source: â€¦ Â· verified on â€¦ Â· Provisional rule\" for each listed check. |\r\n| Fuzzy score never `ok` | âœ… | The existing fast-check property in `evaluate.test.ts` covers this; it is also checked on samples A/B/C (only `same` â†’ ok). |\r\n\r\n**3. Rejection decoder** (`/decode`)\r\n- `src/core/decode.ts` (pure): `RawClassification` (zod: `RejectionCode` enum + confidence 0â€“1), `decodeResult()`. A known code with confidence â‰¥ 0.7 â†’ `matched` with fixed steps from `rejectionCodes.ts`. Otherwise (UNKNOWN, < 0.7, or no AI) â†’ `needs_verification`, showing the UNKNOWN steps and `ASK_AT_OFFICE` (4 bilingual questions); a low-confidence guess appears only as \"It might be: â€¦ please confirm\". `redactForModel()`. `MAX_DECODE_CHARS` is 2000.\r\n- `ai.ts` `classifyRejection()`: text only, `temperature: 0`, prompt `classify-rejection-v1` (it lists the codes and treats the pasted text as data only); zod check, one retry, `{ error }` fallback; never throws.\r\n- `POST /api/decode` (`handleDecode` in `api.ts`): always returns a useful answer, even when the AI is unavailable (`ai: \"ai_unavailable\"` + needs_verification). Bad input â†’ 400 before any AI call.\r\n- UI: `src/app/decode/{page,DecodeApp,DecodeAnswer}.tsx`, Assamese by default with an English toggle; the steps are also shown in the other language (collapsed). Home: a \"Got a rejection? Decode it\" card under the scheme list. Strings are in `i18n.ts` (`decode.*`, both languages).\r\n- Tests: `core/decode.test.ts` (9), `server/classify.test.ts` (4, mocked fetch), `server/apiDecode.test.ts` (4, mocked `ai.ts`), including the backlog's done-when case.\r\n\r\n\r\n**4. `npm run demo:reset`**\r\n- `RuleStore.resetAll()` deletes all rows and resets the id sequence in one transaction. `scripts/demo-reset.mjs` (Node type-stripping imports `store.ts`, so `store.ts` stays the only writer; reads `.env.local` for `KAAGAZ_DB_PATH`).\r\n- A running server picks the reset up too: `syncRegistry()` rebuilds the registry from the built-ins (`resetRegistry()` in `schemes/index.ts`) when it holds a version that is no longer published.\r\n- Tests: `store.test.ts` (+1) and `demoReset.test.ts` (2: fresh process â†’ 3 original schemes at their built-in versions; running process â†’ drops 2.1.0).\r\n\r\n**Also (approved by Claude, under 10 min):** `AgeRange.max` is now optional (no upper limit, e.g. IGNOAPS 60+). Messages read \"60 or older\" / \"à§¬à§¦ à¦¬à¦¾ à¦¤à¦¾à¦¤à¦•à§ˆ à¦¬à§‡à¦›à¦¿\"; the diff view shows \"60+ years\". +1 test.\r\n**Item 5 (polish):** `/` now shows a bilingual \"Loadingâ€¦\" status instead of \"â€¦\" while the catalog loads. I did not do a 360px check (no browser here). New UI uses the same `max-w-xl`, full-width, â‰¥ 48px controls as the existing screens.\r\n\r\n**Results**\r\n- `npm test`: 35 files, **264 passed, 0 failed** (225 before + 39 new). `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`: pass (`/decode` static, `/api/decode` dynamic).\r\n- Live check (`next start`, real Cline API): \"Payment failed: Aadhaar not seeded with bank account\" â†’ `matched AADHAAR_NOT_SEEDED_BANK` 0.98 with Assamese steps; a nonsense message â†’ `UNKNOWN` â†’ needs_verification. The log lines hold only fn/model/promptVersion/inputHash/outcome/ms. Without a key: needs_verification + `ai_unavailable`.\r\n- Passcode live check: with `ADMIN_PASSCODE` set, no header or the wrong one â†’ 401 (list and publish), the right one â†’ 200. Without it, `/admin` shows the \"Demo mode: unprotected\" banner.\r\n- `npm run demo:reset` on the real `data/kaagaz.db` removed the 2 leftover T3 proposals (orunodoi-3 2.1.0, nsap-old-age 1.0.0, both `proposed`); a backup is in `%TEMP%\\kaagaz-before-reset.db`. Home then listed pm-kisan, orunodoi-3, nsap-widow (all 2.0.0), with no Old Age Pension.\r\n\r\n**Open issues**\r\n- The 360px check and the phone click-through of `/`, `/admin` and `/decode` are still not done (no browser automation here).\r\n- The new Assamese strings (`i18n.ts` `decode.*`, `ASK_AT_OFFICE`, the \"or older\" age text) are drafts and need native-speaker review.\r\n- The passcode only protects the API; the `/admin` page itself (demo notice texts) still loads. That's fine, since it holds no data until the passcode is entered.\r\n- `docs/README-draft.md` appeared in the working tree during this run (not created by Cline). It is committed as-is with `git add -A`, like the pre-modified `tasks/NEXT.md` and `.cline-runs/*`.\r\n\r\n**Requests for Claude**\r\n- Should the T3 agent prompt mention that `ageRange.max` may now be omitted (instead of using 120)? `ruleMaintenance.ts` was out of scope, so I left it unchanged.\r\n- Age-banded payments are recorded as future scope in `memory-bank/progress.md`, as you asked.\r\n\r\n","executionId":"4e3a2a87-fe06-4ccd-90f7-a