e: object; schemes: { id: string }[] };\r\n> 81:     expect(Object.keys(out.schemeRule.properties)).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([\"id\", \"version\", \"benefit\", \"ageRange\", \"requirements\"]));\r\n  82:     expect(out.testCase).toBeTruthy();\r\n  83:     expect(out.schemes.map((s) => s.id).sort()).toEqual([\"nsap-widow\", \"orunodoi-3\", \"pm-kisan\"]);\r\n\ntasks/LOG.md:39:190\n  37: \n  38: **Files created (all pure, in `src/core/`)**\n> 39: - `types.ts`: zod schemas `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (with `version`), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Question`, `DocRequirement`, `NameCheckRule`, `FieldCheckRule`, `ExternalCheckRule`, `AgeRange`, `Benefit` (+ `BenefitOverride`), `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n  40: - `schemes/sources.ts` (provenance builders, verifiedOn 2026-10-10), `schemes/pm-kisan.ts`, `schemes/orunodoi-3.ts`, `schemes/nsap-widow.ts`, `schemes/index.ts` (`getScheme`, `listSchemes`, `listSchemeVersions`, `registerScheme`, `questionsFor`).\n  41: - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`: Devanagari and Assamese/Bengali → Latin), `age.ts`, `aadhaar.ts`, `benefit.ts`, `evaluate.ts`, `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts`, `samples.ts` (fake samples A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n\ntasks/LOG.md:162:161\n  160: **Open issues**\n  161: - **`/admin` has no authentication.** Anyone who can reach the server can run the agent (it costs API credits) and publish rules. Fine for the local demo; must be decided before any deployment.\n> 162: - The engine supports one flat benefit amount, so IGNOAPS's ₹500 for 80+ is a note, not computed. The agent also used 120 as an upper age placeholder, because `AgeRange.max` is required.\n  163: - A live run takes about 20–60 s; a model timeout can cost one retry (seen once in the IGNOAPS run).\n  164: - I did not click through `/admin` or `/` in a real browser here (no browser automation). Both were checked through the server-rendered HTML and the APIs on `next start`.\n\ntasks/LOG.md:169:101\n  167: **Requests for Claude**\n  168: - Decide on `/admin` protection for the demo (e.g. a shared passcode in `.env.local`, or local-only), or confirm none.\n> 169: - Should the engine support age-banded benefits (IGNOAPS ₹200 for 60–79, ₹500 for 80+), and should `AgeRange.max` become optional (IGNOAPS has no upper limit)? Both are small schema/engine changes outside T3's scope.\n  170: - Please confirm the two extra `rule_versions` columns (`notice`, `summary`).\n  171: \n\ntasks/LOG.md:206:47\n  204: - Tests: `store.test.ts` (+1) and `demoReset.test.ts` (2: fresh process → 3 original schemes at their built-in versions; running process → drops 2.1.0).\n  205: \n> 206: **Also (approved by Claude, under 10 min):** `AgeRange.max` is now optional (no upper limit, e.g. IGNOAPS 60+). Messages read \"60 or older\" / \"৬০ বা তাতকৈ বেছি\"; the diff view shows \"60+ years\". +1 test.\n  207: **Item 5 (polish):** `/` now shows a bilingual \"Loading…\" status instead of \"…\" while the catalog loads. I did not do a 360px check (no browser here). New UI uses the same `max-w-xl`, full-width, ≥ 48px controls as the existing screens.\n  208: \n\ntasks/LOG.md:222:44\n  220: \n  221: **Requests for Claude**\n> 222: - Should the T3 agent prompt mention that `ageRange.max` may now be omitted (instead of using 120)? `ruleMaintenance.ts` was out of scope, so I left it unchanged.\n  223: - Age-banded payments are recorded as future scope in `memory-bank/progress.md`, as you asked.\n  224: \n","success":true}],"durationMs":111}}
