{"ts":"2026-10-10T12:02:55.257Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm planning to update the prompt to clarify that open-ended age ranges should omit ageRange.max rather than using a placeholder like 120, and bump the prompt version to v2 to reflect this change in logging, plus add a test case to cover it.\n\nNow I'm double-checking the README draft against the actual repo: confirming the cp command works fine on Windows PowerShell, verifying the listed API routes and pages exist, checking that core files like evaluate.ts, store.ts, and ruleMaintenance.ts are present, and validating the claim about running the official Cline CLI by looking at a sample task.md log header.\n\nI also want to be careful about attribution - memory-bank/projectbrief.md was actually created by Cline from Claude's brief, not written directly by Claude, so I should phrase that more precisely. I'm also confirming test counts, the \"publish re-runs every check\" behavior, the MIN_NEW_TESTS=3 rule, and that plan/act mode descriptions match what actually happened in the T0 run, while avoiding unverified claims like checkpoints that aren't mentioned in the draft.\n\nI should double check the Node version requirements too - node:sqlite and TypeScript stripping for demo:reset need Node 22.6+ or 22.18+ unflagged, and I want to verify flags like --disable-warning and --env-file-if-exists are available in the right Node versions before citing them.\n\nSeparately, I want to note attribution clearly: all application code is Cline-authored with Claude providing specs and review, and the policy/rule decisions were cross-checked against government sources, plus flag that docs/README-draft.md was a draft.\n\nI should also verify no commits came from outside Cline runs and double-check the last run's README/agent-prompt fixes are reflected. For secrets, I want to avoid ever printing the key value — I can compute just enough of a prefix locally to grep for it without echoing the full secret.\n\nI'm weighing options for searching the git history and even untracked files for the key without leaking it in output, including checking the tracked .cline-runs logs — if the key shows up there I may not be able to clean it myself and would need to flag it. I also want to check the rest of the rule maintenance test file for prompt-related tests.\n\n"}}
