{"ts":"2026-10-10T12:07:46.798Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now I'm writing the README setup instructions, using `cp` since it works in both bash and PowerShell, avoiding the need for separate Windows/Unix commands.\n\nI also need to fix the actual UI text for the unavailable message, and clarify Node version requirements—settling on something like \"Node 24 (tested with 24.21.0)\" since `demo:reset` needs TypeScript type stripping support that landed around Node 22.18, while keeping the claim modest since I'm not fully certain of the exact version threshold.\n\nFor the copy command, I'll use PowerShell's `copy` to match the existing README style, with a note for macOS/Linux `cp`. I'm double-checking the admin rules API route exists, verifying scripts to add (lint, typecheck, build, smoke tests), and double-checking the runs table—deciding to include the bridge connection test run since it's accurate, and leaving \"checkpoints\" out of the Cline features list since I can't verify it was used. I also need to correct the claim about Claude only writing specs, since memory-bank files were actually created elsewhere too.\n\nFor honest attribution I want to state plainly that Cline wrote all the application code while Claude wrote specs and reviewed, and Das drove decisions and verified rules against government sources. I'll need to re-verify the final test count after running tests, and I should adjust the wording around \"official source\" verification since the code only checks for a source URL in the notice rather than confirming it's truly official.\n\nI'm checking that the citizen-facing app picks up new versions immediately, noting the ADMIN_PASSCODE detail, and confirming the sample documents (A/B/C) and their i18n labels are fine as-is. I'll skip adding README-draft to the docs list since that's mostly Claude's territory.\n\nNow I'm planning to write the README in chunks under 6000 characters, replacing the entire existing content by matching the full old text, then appending further sections afterward.\n\nThe prompt change and its test are done; now I'll update the README, correcting the Windows message text, clarifying the \"verified\" status logic per rulePolicy.ts, and listing setup in PowerShell form with the existing smoke test scripts.\n\n"}}
