erver/apiCheck.test.ts:75:43\n  73:     expect((await check({ ...sample(\"A\"), schemeVersion: \"9.9.9\" })).status).toBe(404);\r\n  74:     expect((await checkPost(post(\"{not json\"))).status).toBe(400);\r\n> 75:     expect((await check({ ...sample(\"A\"), asOfDate: \"2026-02-30\" })).status).toBe(400);\r\n  76:     const fullAadhaar = [{ docType: \"aadhaar\", fields: { aadhaarLast4: \"123456784821\" }, confidence: {} }];\r\n  77:     expect((await check({ ...sample(\"A\"), docs: fullAadhaar })).status).toBe(400);\r\n\ntasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md:8:43\n  6: 2. `src/core/schemes/pm-kisan.ts`, `orunodoi-3.ts`, `nsap-widow.ts`: data validated by `SchemeRule`. Every criterion and benefit has provenance with `status: verified | provisional` exactly as docs/schemes.md marks it. Question text in Assamese + English. Registry: `getScheme(id)`, `listSchemes()`, `registerScheme(rule)` (used by T3).\n  7: 3. `src/core/nameMatch.ts` → `{ level: same | possible_match | initials_only | mismatch, score }` per docs/schemes.md. Normalisation, honorifics, abbreviations, transliteration of Devanagari and Assamese/Bengali script to Latin (basic table), Jaro-Winkler.\n> 8: 4. `src/core/age.ts`: age on an explicit `asOfDate`.\n  9: 5. `src/core/aadhaar.ts`: `maskAadhaar()` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`.\n  10: 6. `src/core/benefit.ts`: `benefitOn(scheme, date)`, supporting time-bounded overrides (needed for the T3 demo).\n\ntasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md:11:61\n  9: 5. `src/core/aadhaar.ts`: `maskAadhaar()` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`.\n  10: 6. `src/core/benefit.ts`: `benefitOn(scheme, date)`, supporting time-bounded overrides (needed for the T3 demo).\n> 11: 7. `src/core/evaluate.ts`: `evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report`. Rules:\n  12:    - verified criterion failed → eligibility `not_eligible`\n  13:    - provisional criterion triggered → `needs_verification` (never not_eligible)\n\ntasks/backlog/T2-main-flow.md:7:97\n  5: 1. `src/server/ai.ts` (the ONLY model caller): `extractDocument(imageBase64, hintDocType?)` → `ExtractedDoc` (zod), per-field confidence, one retry, safe fallback `{ error }`. Cline API (OpenAI-compatible) with image input; if images are rejected, note it under \"Requests for Claude\" and keep manual entry working. Mask Aadhaar inside ai.ts. Never store images.\n  6: 2. `src/core/samples.ts`: samples A/B/C as in memory-bank/projectbrief.md (fake names, `XXXX XXXX 0000`-style Aadhaar).\n> 7: 3. API (`runtime = \"nodejs\"`): `POST /api/extract`, `POST /api/check` (schemeId, docs, answers, asOfDate? → Report).\n  8: 4. UI steps: scheme cards (Assamese names; PM-KISAN marked \"flagship\") → documents (photo per mandatory doc, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm fields (low confidence highlighted) → yes/no questions (big buttons) → **report with TWO verdict banners**: \"Eligibility\" and \"Application readiness\", each 🟢/🔴/🟡/⚪ → check list (reason, where to fix, source link with \"verified on\" date, a \"provisional rule\" badge where relevant) → \"Print cover sheet\".\n  9: 5. Footer on every report: \"We help catch preventable mistakes. We don't guarantee approval; the department decides.\" (Assamese + English).\n\ntasks/LOG.md:79:218\n  77: - `src/i18n.ts`: all fixed UI strings, `as` (default) + `en`, same keys (tested), with doc/office names reused from `labels.ts`.\n  78: - `src/server/ai.ts`: the only model caller. Cline API chat/completions with an `image_url` part, then JSON extraction, zod `RawExtraction`, `toExtractedDoc`, one retry, then `{ error }` (`ai_unavailable` | `ai_failed` | `invalid_image`). `fetch`/`env`/`log` are injectable for tests. Logs `{ model, promptVersion: \"extract-doc-v1\", inputHash (sha256/16), attempt, outcome, ms }` only.\n> 79: - `src/server/api.ts` + `src/app/api/check/route.ts`, `src/app/api/extract/route.ts` (thin). `/api/check` validates with zod (strict `ExtractedDoc`, so a full Aadhaar is rejected), 404 for an unknown scheme/version, `asOfDate` defaults to today in IST. Error bodies hold only paths and codes, never submitted values.\n  80: - UI (`src/app/_components/`): `KaagazApp` (state + steps), `SchemeStep`, `DocsStep` (photo per slot with camera capture, browser downscale to JPEG ≤1600px, \"type it in\", samples A/B/C for the chosen scheme), `ConfirmStep` (low confidence highlighted in amber, \"This is correct\" button), `QuestionsStep` (big Yes/No, \"rule not confirmed\" badge), `ReportStep` + `CheckItem` + `BenefitCard`, `CoverSheet` (print only, masked Aadhaar, no account number), `ui.tsx`, `image.ts`.\n  81: - `scripts/smoke.mjs`: manual smoke test against a running server (not part of `npm test`).\n","success":true}],"durationMs":73}}
